<title>INDIA: India's Century Tex hit by high interest.</title>
<headline>India's Century Tex hit by high interest.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Century Textiles and Industries Ltd said on Tuesday its interest and finance charges jumped by a whopping 218.6 percent to 1.63 billion rupees during the financial year ended March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>Interest cost during the previous year was 510.7 million rupees.</p>
<p>Century said the higher interest burden was due to the fact that its Bagasse-based paper project, a new cement project in Maihar in central Madhya Pradesh state and some other capital expenses have been financed from loans.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
